### 3. How to implement GBM in `see_some_data()`

Geometric Brownian Motion assumes that the percentage change in the stock price is normally distributed. To simulate this step-by-step, we use the standard discrete solution:

$$ S_{t+\Delta t} = S_t \times \exp\left( (\mu - \frac{\sigma^2}{2})\Delta t + \sigma \sqrt{\Delta t} Z \right) $$

